WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710
Hi, in this video we are going to talk
about: what is a LAN? A LAN is a 'local

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:09.120
area network.' So, what does it mean?
Imagine you have your home and you have

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.080
your own wireless router, you got your
desktop connected, your laptop connected

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:18.449
and a printer connected to this router.
And your neighbor has a similar setup. He

00:00:18.449 --> 00:00:23.609
has home router, and desktop is connected,
and he's got two laptops, and they're all

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:29.640
in their own network. So now what happens is this network which is in your home is

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:36.120
a LAN. It is local to your home and this
particular network in your neighbor's

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:41.430
house is a different LAN. So these two
are two different local area networks.

